{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Gender Issues", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Women in Medicine", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 13, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe  routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "the medical profession", "type": "name"}, {"content": "all the different types of doctors of medicine", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The medical profession is one of the best examples of a career field that includes more women now than it did before.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about people who work in medicine.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to stay single", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to not get married", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Many women are now staying single longer and having families later in life.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "approximately", "type": "name"}, {"content": "around, about", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In the United States, approximately one third of doctors are women today. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "caregiver", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone who takes care of another person, such as a young child or an elderly person", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Women have proven themselves to be patient and trustworthy caregivers. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "nursing care ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "assistance for people who need help for a variety of reasons (sickness, age, disability, etc.)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Women have provided nursing care for centuries. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to figure", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be part of something; to be recognized for something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Men have figured more prominently in the written history of medicine.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be involved", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to participate in something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Historically, women have been more involved in healthcare than men. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le13ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect vs. Simple Past Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about generalities from past which are relevant at present. <br />  You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event not connected to the present.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you use the Present Perfect there is a connection between what happened in the past and now. You use time markers like<span class=\"italic\"> for, since</span> and <span class=\"italic\">ever</span> with the Present Perfect. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use the Simple Past, the time is always past. You use time markers with the past like <span class=\"italic\"> then, ago, yesterday, when I was\u2026</span> with the Simple Past. To form the Present Perfect tense, you use have/has + the past participle of the base form of the verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Historically, women have been more involved in health care than men.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They have proven themselves to be patient and trustworthy caregivers.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Comparatives and Superlatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use comparative adjectives to compare yourself to another      person. <br> You use a superlative adjectives to compare yourself or          something to a group of people.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can compare things using the words <span class=\"italic\">more (than)</span> or <span class=\"italic\">less (than)</span>.  <br> You can also use adjectives to compare things. Some adjectives        change to different words in the comparative and superlative form.<br> With one-syllable words, you add <span class=\"strong\">-er</span> to the adjective to make the       comparative form. You add <span class=\"strong\">-est</span> to the adjective to make the         superlative form.  <br> With words of two or more syllables, you add the word<span class=\"italic\"> more</span> before          the adjective or adverb in the comparative form. You add <span class=\"italic\">the most</span>      before the adjective or the adverb in the superlative form.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjective or  Adverb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Comparative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Superlative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"--\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" the most\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"--\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"less\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" the least\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"good\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"better\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" the best\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"fast\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"faster\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" the fastest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"involved\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" more involved\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" the most involved\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"prominently\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more prominently\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" the most prominently\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"accurately\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" more accurately\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" the most accurately\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "The medical profession is one of the best examples of a career field that includes more women now than it did before. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Men have figured more prominently in the written history of medicine because most of the old manuscripts found have been written by men.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Choose 10 different countries.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Go online. Find out the percentage of female doctors in each country.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write your list in order from the country with the most female doctors (#1) to the country with the least (#10).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss your list with a partner. Together, try to explain the results.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I do research on the Internet.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I complete a list of countries.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I order the list according to the percentage of female doctors.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss the list with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn6le13ob06re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn6le13ob06re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn6le13ob06re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"image": "engenn6le13ob06re2img01.jpg", "text": "In 1849, American-born Elizabeth Blackwell graduated from medical school in Geneva and became the first woman doctor in history.", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"image": "engenn6le13ob06re2img02.jpg", "text": "The medical profession is one of the best examples of a career field that includes more women now than it did before. There was a time when medicine was considered too time-consuming for a woman who wanted to have a family. As many women are now staying single longer and having families later in life, more women than before are choosing to become doctors. In the United States, approximately one-third of doctors are women today.", "time": "9750", "id": 2}, {"image": "engenn6le13ob06re2img03.jpg", "text": "Historically, women have been more involved in healthcare than men. They have provided nursing care, delivered babies and prepared home remedies for centuries. They have proven themselves to be patient and trustworthy caregivers. Men have figured more prominently in the written history of medicine because most of the old manuscripts found have been written by men, and because women weren't allowed into medical school until the mid-1800s.", "time": "35500", "id": 3}]}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about personal qualities and family life.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can discuss experiences I've had or haven't had.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can compare two things or people and describe the quality of an object or a person.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Do you think both men and women have equal opportunity to work in healthcare? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Have you thought about working in healthcare? In what job?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "The doctor is in!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " In this article, Sally explores gender issues in the medical profession.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "